/-!
# Original fibre lifts and their genuine negative Dolbeault primitives

This package restricts the actual family cover and cocycle to each
original period torus by the original fibre inclusion. The original
family lifts have constant base coordinate and their fibre components
are holomorphic in the unchanged native torus atlas. Their quotient
projections are the original points of that same native torus.

The negative marked real-linear primitive on these literal local
lifts gives actual smooth sections satisfying exactly
`t_j - t_i = inclusion(c_ij)`. Their original native Dolbeault
differentials are the restrictions of one actual closed constant
global coefficient pair, whose marked Haar means are the negative
literal antiholomorphic coefficients of the original primitive.

No separation property of the base is assumed. The only holomorphic
base hypothesis is the original manifold structure. This package does
not assert a comparison of extension classes or a higher-direct-image
isomorphism; it supplies the actual local sections and their equations
needed for those subsequent genuine comparisons.
-/
